  "schema_change": {
    "location": "$defs.ProofTrace.properties.summary_coverage, appended to ProofTrace.required",
    "shape": "oneOf[null, array of closed {body:$ref U, stop: array of boolean minItems 4 maxItems 4, has_data: boolean}, required all three, additionalProperties false]",
    "not_in_schema": "No minItems on the coverage array: an empty array is a G3 cardinality failure (I57 s4 G3), not a G1 shape failure. No new $defs name, policy id, signature or hash domain. A $comment documents order and null meaning; shape walkers ignore it.",
    "vocabulary": "Only oneOf/null/array/items/minItems/maxItems/object/boolean/$ref already used by the pinned schema walkers."
  },
  "coverage_derivation": {
    "method": "I57 s2 per selected case from its own source layout (present/non_input_present per kind), adaptive::body_extent order via rp._extent, E=selected resolution_scale, floor (null at p128), verification record and certified_bound; asserted in the build: D=false (only constrained displacement/rotation rows are input-derived, all prescribed +0), the 16-vector feasibility rule admits the attested stop bits, estimate/charge rosters equal the derivation, has_data agrees with the free-DOF/nonzero-term constraints, record bound non-null iff has_data, theta +0 for no-data, data_blocks=0 iff no has_data.",
    "ordinary_prepared_synthetic / dense": "One body, all four kinds present with non-input rows, L=1 (nodes 0 and x=1), E force=moment>0, p128 so charge=estimate=[T,T], floor null. Stop bits are the synthetic attestation already carried by the existing four-entry stop_rule: [T,T,T,T] (feasible). Six distinct nonzero free-DOF nodal terms at node 1, certified_bound present, data_blocks=1: has_data=true.",
    "ordinary_prepared_no_data_synthetic": "Case 0 with every authored primitive-load magnitude set to 0: nodal terms +0 (K4SRC rehashed through rp._native_source_encoding; K4STF unchanged), all solved rows/maxima/enclosure/headlines +0 (displacement headline moves to the identity-tie winner node:fixture-root), projection outcomes +0, verification resolution/theta +0, bound null, data_blocks 0; stop_rule/estimate/charge/certified_bound empty; body_scales +0; every quantity row absolute_verified with scale and bound +0. Coverage [{body:0, stop:[F,F,F,F], has_data:false}]. Work magnitudes and the solver-mode metadata text are copied synthetic attestations, not a zero-load execution."
  },
  "hash_scopes": "Rehashed only through the test harness apply_mutation(rehash='all'), i.e. the reader's own _hash/_source_hash/_preparation_payload, as I58 did. For the two existing cases only receipt_sha256 changed; publication, preparation and source-identity hashes and every other byte are unchanged (asserted). The new case additionally has its own invocation digest (tests.rebind_invocation method), K4SRC digest, publication, source and receipt hashes.",
